        "lua": "function()\n    local window = hl.get_active_window()\n    if not window then\n        return\n    end\n    if window.floating then\n        hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.window.move({ x = 30, y = 0, relative = true }))\n    else\n        hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.window.swap({ direction = \"right\" }))\n    end\nend",
        "why_lua": "Asks the compositor whether the focused window is floating and picks one of two dispatchers. The v1 bind answered the same question by running `hyprctl activewindow -j | jq -r .floating` through bash and grepping for the string true, which needed two external programs to ask a yes-or-no question the Lua API answers with a boolean field (LuaBindingsQuery.cpp:129-138, LuaWindow.cpp:101-102)."
